# U-Boot config fragment for the PB2 CAN Carrier image.
# Verify against the pinned U-Boot tree (manifests/sources.lock:
# beagleboard/u-boot @ v2026.01-am62-pocketbeagle2) with
# scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh before first build.
#
# Boot flow (confirmed against beagleboard/image-builder
# tools/hwpack/pocketbeagle2-swap.conf): PB2 images boot via U-Boot
# distro_bootcmd + extlinux.conf, not the legacy uEnv.txt mechanism.
# extlinux.conf's actual template (extlinux_firmware_file =
# .../bb-u-boot-pocketbeagle2/microsd-extlinux-w-swap.conf) is produced by
# image-builder's own u-boot packaging stage from the pinned
# beagleboard/u-boot source -- "bb-u-boot-pocketbeagle2" is a build-local
# package name in that pipeline, not a separate external repo (searched;
# none found under that name). TODO: locate the exact template within
# image-builder's u-boot packaging stage and confirm the FDTOVERLAYS/APPEND
# lines below land in it. Requirement: UART0 pinmux + console output in
# SPL/U-Boot at 115200 8N1 without disabling MAIN_UART6 hardware (work
# order §7.1), and deterministic carrier overlay loading with a visible
# boot failure if it is missing/fails to apply (work order §7.1, §12).

CONFIG_CONS_INDEX=1
CONFIG_BAUDRATE=115200
CONFIG_OF_LIBFDT_OVERLAY=y
CONFIG_OF_BOARD_FIXUP=y

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# extlinux.conf additions
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Add to the extlinux.conf entry (or the microsd-extlinux template in
# bb-u-boot-pocketbeagle2) so the carrier overlay loads on every boot and
# a missing/failed overlay aborts the boot rather than silently booting
# without carrier hardware (work order §7.1, §12):
#
#   FDTOVERLAYS /boot/dtbs/${uname_r}/overlays/k3-am62-pocketbeagle2-can-carrier.dtbo
#
# U-Boot's distro-boot FDTOVERLAYS handling already aborts distro_bootcmd
# with a visible error if a listed .dtbo is missing or fails to apply;
# confirm that behavior against the pinned tree during bring-up (work
# order §12: "A missing/failed overlay must be visible in boot logs and
# treated as a release failure").
#
# APPEND kernel command line (work order §5.5):
#
#   earlycon=ns16550a,mmio32,0x02800000,115200n8 console=ttyS7,115200n8 console=ttyS2,115200n8
#
# earlycon address 0x02800000 is main_uart0's MMIO base (verified against
# k3-am62-main.dtsi: `main_uart0: serial@2800000`) -- this half is
# address-based and does not depend on enumeration order.
#
# The `console=ttySN` device names ARE enumeration-order-dependent and are
# only a best guess from the DT aliases (serial7 = main_uart0, serial2 =
# main_uart6 in the stock PB2 DTS): TODO confirm the real /dev/ttySN
# mapping from `dmesg | grep ttyS` on first boot and correct these two
# values before considering CON-01/CON-02 (work order §11) satisfied --
# this is exactly the ambiguity work order §5.5 calls out ("document and
# test the exact kernel command line ... instead of relying on incidental
# enumeration order"). The first `console=` argument wins for
# /dev/console; list UART0 first since it is the required primary.
